––– comment –––
Regression for #5129: NULLs survive Buddy's JSON roundtrip and empty JOINs preserve SELECT columns.
––– block: ../base/start-searchd-with-buddy –––
––– input –––
mysql -h0 -P9306 -e "DROP TABLE IF EXISTS gh5129_a; DROP TABLE IF EXISTS gh5129_b; CREATE TABLE gh5129_a (t TEXT) min_infix_len='2'; CREATE TABLE gh5129_b (aid BIGINT, price FLOAT, qty INT); INSERT INTO gh5129_a (id,t) VALUES (1,'one'); INSERT INTO gh5129_b (id,aid,price,qty) VALUES (2,2,19.99,7);"
––– output –––
––– comment –––
HTTP SQL must represent unmatched numeric JOIN attributes as explicit JSON nulls.
––– input –––
curl -sS 'http://127.0.0.1:9308/sql?mode=raw' --data-urlencode "query=SELECT id,gh5129_b.price,gh5129_b.qty FROM gh5129_a LEFT JOIN gh5129_b ON gh5129_a.id=gh5129_b.aid WHERE MATCH('one')" | grep -oE '"gh5129_b\.(price|qty)":null'
––– output –––
"gh5129_b.price":null
"gh5129_b.qty":null
––– comment –––
The MySQL response after fuzzy processing must contain real SQL NULL markers for float and int.
––– input –––
mysql -h0 -P9306 --xml -e "SELECT id,gh5129_b.price,gh5129_b.qty FROM gh5129_a LEFT JOIN gh5129_b ON gh5129_a.id=gh5129_b.aid WHERE MATCH('one') OPTION fuzzy=1,preserve=1" | grep -oE 'name="gh5129_b\.(price|qty)" xsi:nil="true"'
––– output –––
name="gh5129_b.price" xsi:nil="true"
name="gh5129_b.qty" xsi:nil="true"
––– comment –––
Selecting only a NULL right-hand column must still return one row with a real SQL NULL.
––– input –––
mysql -h0 -P9306 --xml -e "SELECT gh5129_b.price FROM gh5129_a LEFT JOIN gh5129_b ON gh5129_a.id=gh5129_b.aid WHERE MATCH('one') OPTION fuzzy=1,preserve=1" | grep -oE 'name="gh5129_b.price" xsi:nil="true"'
––– output –––
name="gh5129_b.price" xsi:nil="true"
––– comment –––
A NULL before a non-NULL column must not shift values in HTTP or MySQL results.
––– input –––
curl -sS 'http://127.0.0.1:9308/sql?mode=raw' --data-urlencode "query=SELECT gh5129_b.price,id FROM gh5129_a LEFT JOIN gh5129_b ON gh5129_a.id=gh5129_b.aid WHERE MATCH('one')" | grep -oE '\{"gh5129_b\.price":[^{}]+\}'
––– output –––
{"gh5129_b.price":null,"id":1}
––– input –––
mysql -h0 -P9306 --xml -e "SELECT gh5129_b.price,id FROM gh5129_a LEFT JOIN gh5129_b ON gh5129_a.id=gh5129_b.aid WHERE MATCH('one') OPTION fuzzy=1,preserve=1" 2>&1 | grep -oE '<field name="[^"]+"( xsi:nil="true" />|>[^<]*</field>)|^ERROR.*'
––– output –––
<field name="gh5129_b.price" xsi:nil="true" />
<field name="id">1</field>
––– comment –––
An empty INNER JOIN must report only requested columns, with or without fuzzy processing.
––– input –––
mysql -h0 -P9306 --column-type-info -vvv -e "SELECT id,t,gh5129_b.price FROM gh5129_a JOIN gh5129_b ON gh5129_a.id=gh5129_b.aid WHERE MATCH('one')" | sed -nE 's/^Field[[:space:]]+[0-9]+:[[:space:]]+`([^`]+)`$/\1/p'
––– output –––
id
t
gh5129_b.price
––– input –––
mysql -h0 -P9306 --column-type-info -vvv -e "SELECT id,t,gh5129_b.price FROM gh5129_a JOIN gh5129_b ON gh5129_a.id=gh5129_b.aid WHERE MATCH('one') OPTION fuzzy=1,preserve=1" | sed -nE 's/^Field[[:space:]]+[0-9]+:[[:space:]]+`([^`]+)`$/\1/p'
––– output –––
id
t
gh5129_b.price
––– comment –––
Empty results from a single table must preserve SELECT columns too.
––– input –––
mysql -h0 -P9306 --column-type-info -vvv -e "SELECT id,t FROM gh5129_a WHERE MATCH('missing')" | sed -nE 's/^Field[[:space:]]+[0-9]+:[[:space:]]+`([^`]+)`$/\1/p'
––– output –––
id
t
––– comment –––
An empty limited GROUP_CONCAT must return its SELECT columns without an error.
––– input –––
mysql -h0 -P9306 --column-type-info -vvv -e "SELECT qty,GROUP_CONCAT(id ORDER BY id DESC LIMIT 2) gc FROM gh5129_b WHERE qty=0 GROUP BY qty" 2>&1 | sed -nE 's/^Field[[:space:]]+[0-9]+:[[:space:]]+`([^`]+)`$/\1/p; /^ERROR/p'
––– output –––
qty
gc
––– comment –––
An empty search over tables with different schemas must keep the requested column in parallel search.
––– input –––
mysql -h0 -P9306 -e "DROP TABLE IF EXISTS gh5129_s1; DROP TABLE IF EXISTS gh5129_s2; CREATE TABLE gh5129_s1 (t TEXT, x INT); CREATE TABLE gh5129_s2 (t TEXT, y INT); INSERT INTO gh5129_s1 (id,t,x) VALUES (1,'one',1); INSERT INTO gh5129_s2 (id,t,y) VALUES (2,'one',2);"
––– output –––
––– input –––
for i in $(seq 1 20); do mysql -h0 -P9306 --column-type-info -vvv -e "SELECT id,x FROM gh5129_s1,gh5129_s2 WHERE MATCH('missing')" 2>&1 | sed -nE 's/^Field[[:space:]]+[0-9]+:[[:space:]]+`([^`]+)`$/\1/p; /^ERROR/p'; done | sort -u
––– output –––
id
x
